31
00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:14.440
soispoke: And you can pack quite a lot of them, because right now, you know, the only limit is, is 8KB. I think it would have to change anyways with frames, but let's say, let's keep it, like, let's keep the simple model in mind.

32
00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:19.450
soispoke: You can fit a ton of transactions within each IL today.

33
00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:26.429
soispoke: And so the first thing you can maybe think about, and maybe, probably, like, the most important thing is, like, can…

34
00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:30.869
soispoke: you know, PQ transactions actually fit, in… in inclusion lists.

35
00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:37.750
soispoke: And I think, for now, the answer is yes, because…

36
00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:45.599
soispoke: well, so far, you know, PQ signatures on the EL will be on the order of…

37
00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:52.110
soispoke: Well, I've heard, you know, from 5 to 7 kilobytes, I guess, as approximations, which is quite huge.

38
00:10:52.120 --> 00:11:08.949
soispoke: And so worst case scenario, well, I mean, yeah, probably the actual sort of, like, lead case scenario is that we will only be able to include one PQ transaction per inclusion list, if things stay as they are today.

39
00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.939
soispoke: And so some of you might think, yeah, it's not great, or not enough.

40
00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:17.680
soispoke: But what's nice is that, you know,

41
00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.689
