soispoke: generally, I feel like, you know, at first, like, only a few people would want to, sort of, like, sign using PQ6, because they would be quite costly anyways, and, having the opportunity to include 16,

48
00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:28.260
soispoke: of those per block is pretty good, I think, but also curious to hear if people think it's not enough, or…

49
00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.260
soispoke: Oh, it's… it's not worth it.

50
00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:42.230
soispoke: And then, yeah, what, like, actually changes the game, and it's, like, to actually sort of, like… needs quite a lot of the modifications and everything, because…

51
00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:52.919
soispoke: I need to… I would have needed to size it a lot differently if we… if I wanted to actually make it fit at scale. It's when we want to include proofs,

52
00:12:53.040 --> 00:13:05.120
soispoke: into ILs, or, like, when we basically want to include much more than 16 PQ transactions in ILS, then we need each ILT to come with its proof, and a proof is huge.

53
00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:13.700
